    "hints": [
        "For every left endpoint <code>l</code>, use two sliding windows to find the earliest right endpoint containing at least <code>k</code> distinct numbers and the earliest right endpoint containing at least <code>k + 1</code> distinct numbers. This lets you determine in <code>O(1)</code> whether a query contains exactly <code>k</code> distinct numbers.",
        "Assign each distinct value a random bitmask and build prefix XORs. The XOR over a subarray is zero when every value occurs an even number of times, with overwhelming probability. After preprocessing, each generated query can therefore be answered in <code>O(1)</code>."
